The points \((0, P(0)), (1, P(1)), (2, P(2)), (3, P(3)), (4, P(4))\) lie on a straight line. This implies that the probabilities form an arithmetic progression.
K = P(1) - P(0) = P(2) - P(1) = P(3) - P(2) = P(4) - P(3)
From this, we can express each probability in terms of \(K\) and \(P(0)\):
P(1) = K + P(0)
P(2) = 2K + P(0)
P(3) = 3K + P(0)
P(4) = 4K + P(0)
The sum of all probabilities must be 1:
P(0) + P(1) + P(2) + P(3) + P(4) = 1
\Rightarrow P(0) + (K + P(0)) + (2K + P(0)) + (3K + P(0)) + (4K + P(0)) = 1
\Rightarrow 5P(0) + 10K = 1 \quad \text{(Equation 1)}
The mean of \(X\) is given as \(\frac{5}{2}\):
\sum_{x=0}^{4} xP(x) = 0 \cdot P(0) + 1 \cdot P(1) + 2 \cdot P(2) + 3 \cdot P(3) + 4 \cdot P(4) = \frac{5}{2}
\Rightarrow (K + P(0)) + 2(2K + P(0)) + 3(3K + P(0)) + 4(4K + P(0)) = \frac{5}{2}
\Rightarrow K + P(0) + 4K + 2P(0) + 9K + 3P(0) + 16K + 4P(0) = \frac{5}{2}
\Rightarrow 30K + 10P(0) = \frac{5}{2} \quad \text{(Equation 2)}
Now we solve Equation 1 and Equation 2 simultaneously.
From Equation 1: \(5P(0) = 1 - 10K\)
Multiply Equation 1 by 2: \(10P(0) + 20K = 2\)
Substitute \(10P(0) = 2 - 20K\) into Equation 2:
30K + (2 - 20K) = \frac{5}{2}
10K + 2 = \frac{5}{2}
10K = \frac{5}{2} - 2 = \frac{5 - 4}{2} = \frac{1}{2}
\therefore K = \frac{1}{20}
Substitute \(K = \frac{1}{20}\) back into Equation 1:
5P(0) + 10\left(\frac{1}{20}\right) = 1
